# Vendored canonical skin/appearance contract pin.
#
# Rule: these files are byte copies from the `contracts` repository. A change to
# any vendored file MUST update its sha256 here, and the copy must be re-taken
# from the tag named below. Do not edit a vendored schema by hand.
#
# v0.14.0 adds the optional `surface.overlay` paint/geometry role for layer-shell overlays (the wallpaper selector); it is additive, so manifests without it stay valid. v0.12.0 made `surface.window` a required sixth surface role (bg, border,
# border-width, radius, padding, shadow, blur, opacity) and adds the unitless
# `[0,1]` opacity value type. It expands the appearance host allowlist from the
# five rectangle paths to seven: `surface.window.radius`,
# `surface.window.border-width`, `surface.panel.radius`,
# `surface.panel.border-width`, `surface.card.radius`, `surface.control.radius`
# and `surface.cell.radius`. Window padding and opacity are never delegable,
# `surface.pill.radius` stays explicit, and no gap, type, paint, colour, state
# or layout path is delegable. The three appearance schemas are the canonical
# set for this class: `appearance-manifest` (the v2 TOML/JSON manifest envelope
# with the optional root `host` policy), `appearance-json` (the resolved
# tokens.json document; mode and host values already applied) and
# `appearance-artifact` (appearance.json metadata). The generation manifest
# schema is vendored for contract-byte parity and records the same seven
# delegated paths in its optional host snapshot; this class emits
# skin/appearance documents, not generations, and never writes an artifact
# path. The three frozen v1 skin schemas are vendored at the same tag for
# provenance; this class no longer emits v1 manifests. All lengths are unitless
# JSON numbers rendered as CSS px, letter-spacing renders as em and font-weight
# stays unitless; only `surface.window.opacity` is a unitless [0,1] number.
